\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {3}{\ignorespaces  Qualitative motivation for the dual-view encoder. For representative UCR tasks, we visualize real training examples nearest to their class centroids, together with their raw sequences, ordered temporal patches, and morphology-map representations. The temporal view preserves ordered patch-level evolution, whereas the morphology view exposes local subsequence shapes and cross-window structural transitions through a two-dimensional waveform map. }}{5}{figure.3}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:dual-view-motivation}{{3}{5}{Qualitative motivation for the dual-view encoder. For representative UCR tasks, we visualize real training examples nearest to their class centroids, together with their raw sequences, ordered temporal patches, and morphology-map representations. The temporal view preserves ordered patch-level evolution, whereas the morphology view exposes local subsequence shapes and cross-window structural transitions through a two-dimensional waveform map}{figure.3}{}}
